Based on my observations, the key insight is that **milestones use `coordinate_frame="spawn_relative"`**, meaning the evaluator automatically converts spawn-relative offsets to absolute coords. So I don't need to know the absolute coordinates — I just need to know the offsets from spawn.

Since the commands use `~` (relative to player position at execution time), and the evaluator spawns the player at the same position where commands are executed, the spawn-relative coordinates ARE the `~` offsets used in the commands.

So:
- **Packed ice center**: spawn-relative (9, 2, 9) — center of the tower at mid-height
- **Sandstone wall center**: spawn-relative (14, 1.5, 9) — center of the wall structure

Now I have all the information needed to design the milestones.

